From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Haoze <90812991+HaozeG@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 13:54:38 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] [shvla] ISS ISA tables: nseq tag on scalar FP
 instructions with an integer operand (SIMULATOR_NOTES #10)

Scalar .s/.h/.ah/.b feq flt fle fcvt.w fcvt.wu fcvt.<fmt>.w fcvt.<fmt>.wu fmv.x fclass fmv.<fmt>.x
lacked the nseq tag that the .d versions have, so they were queued in the FPU
sequence buffer and the integer core read the destination register before the
FP subsystem wrote it (late write-back clobbers newer values). Mirrors Rv32d.

Two places: isa_riscv_gen.py and isa_smallfloats.py in the patched nested core
working tree, and two new file sections in soft_hier/gvsoc_core.patch (applies
without fuzz to pristine nested core HEAD bda268a4, cmp-identical).
Evidence: LOG G3.2-diag (rung c H/G/OUT, rungs 3-5 inf/nan after the first
scalar FP row op). The author's gvsoc_snitch_fp_int_nseq.patch was not
available; tag set reconstructed from SIMULATOR_NOTES #10.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
